# gitattributes.proposed - DRAFT v4 (NARROW) for review. Lesetja copies it to .gitattributes himself.
#
# Deliberately narrow: NO `* text=auto` and NO rule for *.mq5/*.mqh/*.mq4 or anything under
# mql5/. Git's own heuristics keep treating MQL5 sources as they are today (a UTF-16 file
# with NUL bytes is detected as binary and left alone), and nothing is renormalised.
#
# Repo state read on the laptop (2026-10-11, `git ls-files --eol`): 89 tracked files,
# 88 i/lf + 1 i/none (empty desk/tests/__init__.py), 0 i/crlf, 0 i/mixed, 0 -text;
# no UTF-16 or BOM MQL5 files; no binary-type files tracked. The only .cmd files
# (desk/keeper.cmd, desk/link.cmd, desk/reseal.cmd) are already i/lf w/crlf, so the
# CRLF rule below changes no committed content and no working-tree bytes on the laptop.
# VERIFY after copying: `git add --renormalize . && git status` shows nothing to commit.

# Existing rules, copied unchanged from the current .gitattributes
deploy/*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/*.service text eol=lf
deploy/*.timer text eol=lf
deploy/*.example text eol=lf

# Windows scripts: CRLF in every checkout, on every OS (cmd.exe misreads labels in LF files;
# config_guard.py also fails any .cmd/.bat/.ps1 with a bare LF or lone CR)
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never text: compiled MetaTrader files, presets, media, executables, archives
*.ex4 binary
*.ex5 binary
*.set binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.jar binary
